WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.320
Both teams are in position!

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:08.200
It's the finals for Football Frontier International Vision 2's Asia district preliminaries!

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:14.520
The second half between Japan's Inazuma Japan and Uzbekistan's Storm Wolf is about to begin!

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.850
The first half ended at 2-1 with Storm Wolf in the lead!

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.580
Will it be Inazuma Japan or Storm Wolf to win and move on to the world?!

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.980
Go, Inazuma Japan!

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.040
Don't lose to Storm Wolf!

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.800
Guys, let's start by taking back a point first!

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:32.630
Yeah!

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.090
As if that will go down well.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.340
I won't let them steal any more goals!

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.740
Storm Wolf moves up!

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:27.710
Matatagi!

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.170
They're completely different from the first half.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.180
Their power has increased by 37%!

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:40.760
Leave this to me!

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.050
They got through Nozaki!

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.470
Aaron!

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:46.680
I'll stop you!

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.350
They got through Kusaka!

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.610
The second half has barely begun and Storm Wolf has bared their fangs!

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.420
Surprised?

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.880
This is how we play when we're just a tiny bit serious.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.400
All right, let's work with each other!

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.120
Steal the ball and bring it up through passing!

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:08.950
Loran!

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.170
Manabe-kun, let's stop them together! I'll go from the front!

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:17.630
I'll go 32 degrees from the right at 1.2 times the speed!

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.550
Silk Road!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.970
He gets through!

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.270
You won't stop us with defense like that!

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.530
Storm Wolf's attack can't be stopped!

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:35.770
What's wrong, Inazuma Japan! Your momentum from the first half is gone!

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.030
It's no use... They're just too powerful!

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.030
Coach Kuroiwa!

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:44.530
Give it up already.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:48.770
We'll never give up! If we all work together...

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:50.580
Aaron!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.580
Shindou-san!

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.370
Storm Wolf has the upper hand in this match!

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:02.470
The score is 2-1 with Storm Wolf in the lead!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.680
Will it end this way with them winning?!

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.680
I won't lose here!

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:12.420
We trained so hard! If we all work together...

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.730
One point. First get one point, then we can catch up to them!

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:16.730
We'll stop them no matter what!

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:22.360
Zaul!

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.150
Inazuma Japan can't find an opening for a counterattack!

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.870
They get past Morimura!

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:34.830
I'll protect the goal!

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:36.930
Dmitri!

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:38.630
Bring it!

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.510
What?! A feint?!

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.640
It's in!

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.600
Storm Wolf makes another point!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.620
This goal is a big one!

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:56.600
Storm Wolf has widened the point difference by 2 once again!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.110
It's no use... They're way too powerful for us!

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.820
We can't win after all...

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.460
It went in...

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:07.040
Hayato-niichan was right...

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.880
It's still a 2-point difference! We're just warming up!

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.750
Guys...

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.130
It's okay! A chance will come to us if we don't give up trying!

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:25.800
But if we can't even touch the ball...

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:30.060
I'd hate to lose, but we've done our best.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.970
We've made it this far. No one will look down on us for it.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:39.560
No!

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.170
I don't want us to lose like this!

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:44.030
I won't give up!

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.040
But Captain...

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:49.080
I understand how you feel, but some people are just better than others.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.850
That's reality.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:56.460
I don't want to calculate it, but the probability of us winning is a low percentage.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.040
Does that give us an excuse to give up?!

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:01.910
We won't know how it will turn out until we've fought to the last second!

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.260
I won't give up!

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:07.550
Because... I don't want this to be our last match!

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.720
The last match?

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.550
I see... You're right.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:17.190
If we lose this match, there will be no need for Inazuma Japan anymore.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.940
Coach will grant us our contract terms and we'll all go our separate ways...

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.900
The last match...

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.480
Does it matter, really? Even if we lose, we'll get what we want in our contracts.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.620
I know that!

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.800
I know that, but I just can't let it end like this!

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.620
Joining this team helped me to face myself for the first time in my life.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:50.880
By meeting Captain and playing soccer with everyone...

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.880
<i>So this is what it means to be strong, huh?</i>

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.940
<i>I think I figured out 1 millimeter of how that feels like.</i>

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:09.020
I don't know if it was really because of soccer or not...

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:12.600
But if I stop here, I'll lose something...

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.450
I feel as if there's still something left for us to do!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.460
I think so, too...

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:23.310
Until now, all I thought about was making myself look good.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.420
But that feeling I had when I worked together with everyone to win...

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.350
<i>I am not... scared of failing!</i>

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:46.060
That goes for us too.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.440
<i>Morimura!</i>

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.310
<i>You're able to stop him!</i>

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:52.950
<i>Me...?</i>

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.950
<i>I  { \i0}know<i> you can do it!</i></i>

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:11.080
Let's do this, everyone! We've made it this far already.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.370
I want to go even further than where we are right now.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:14.890
I don't want to lose in a place like this!

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:17.260
Ibuki...

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.570
Even further...

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:21.060
Yeah... Let's do it, everyone!

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:24.820
Guys...

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.710
The match resumes with Inazuma Japan's kickoff!

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:34.030
The score is 3-1 with Stom Wolf in the lead!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.820
They still have the motivation to fight?

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:38.800
I'll compliment you for that, at least.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:40.830
But it all ends here.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.210
Why, you...!

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:49.840
A loose ball!

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.050
Leave it to me!

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:54.340
Over here!

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:55.460
Manabe!

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.600
Inazuma Japan is keeping the ball!

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.350
They don't know when to quit.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.060
Sakura!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:06.980
I'll stop you!

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.820
We'll win this match no matter what.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.730
I won't make this our last game!

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.200
Beautiful Hoop!

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.420
Nozaki uses a hissatsu technique!

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:28.710
Kusaka!

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.760
Brutal Head!

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.020
It's in!

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:48.650
Inazuma Japan catches up by one point again!

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:50.110
All right!

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:52.320
That's it, Inazuma Japan!

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:52.320
Go, go!

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.330
Sakura!

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.600
Yeah! I finally did a hissatsu technique!

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:58.570
Yeah!

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.240
One more point to go!

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:02.600
We can do this!

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:04.040
Yeah!

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:08.930
I didn't expect her to have a hissatsu technique like that. I let my guard down.

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:11.350
No, this is their real strength.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.280
Don't you get it? They're determined.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:18.710
They're putting everything they have on the line for this match.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:24.460
If we don't put our full power into this match too, we will lose.

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:28.840
And don't tell me that you've forgotten.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:32.810
If we lose this match, there is no place left for us to go.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:42.110
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.370
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:51.860
Inazuma Japan takes back a point to make the score 3-2!

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.880
Now, will they use this momentum to catch up?!

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.130
The kickoff by Storm Wolf and the match resumes!

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:01.970
Zaul!

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.100
I'll stop them!

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:07.880
Loran!

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:09.100
Aaron!

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:12.600
What's going on? They got even speedier!

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.610
They finally got serious.

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:18.360
We'll win no matter what!

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:21.820
They get past Morimura!

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:22.950
Minaho!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.700
Trace Press!

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.640
Minaho covers her to steal back the ball!

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.290
Inazuma Japan isn't giving in!

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:38.050
True Mach Wind!

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:40.510
Twist Reach!

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:48.350
This is turning into a fierce game!

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.270
Neither side is giving in!

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.790
<i>Soccer is a living thing.</i>

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:05.700
<i>It's a wild beast that will attack you if you look away from it.</i>

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.640
<i>If you don't want to be swallowed up, don't look away.</i>

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:09.910
<i>Keep your eyes on everything around you.</i>

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:14.680
Now, not much time is left!

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:18.090
The score is 3-2 with Storm Wolf still in the lead.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.790
Will they end up winning?!

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.340
Guys...

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.730
Storm Wolf breaks through!

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:28.850
They're completely free!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.020
Ibuki!

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:31.370
I got this!

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:33.310
I can stop shoots from him!

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:37.940
What?!

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:40.320
Gold Fever!

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.240
It's in!

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:53.250
Storm Wolf has a 2-point lead once again!

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.750
There's hardly any time remaining!

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:58.130
Will this point be what decides this match?!

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.130
No way...

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.190
We couldn't catch up...

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.550
Is this the end for us?

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:10.810
What's wrong, guys?

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:13.020
It's not over yet.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.520
We want to move ahead even further, don't we?

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:18.100
But it's a 2-point difference...

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:23.570
We're short on time, and it's not only 1 point we have to take back but 2...

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:27.860
Then we'll get 2 points at the same time!

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:30.880
2 at the same time?!

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:32.620
Yeah! We can catch up that way!

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:36.060
But Captain, this isn't baseball.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:37.930
We can't get 2 points at the same time.

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:40.680
We won't know that until we try!

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.460
But it's just not...

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:43.480
Wait.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.970
It's possible.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.970
It's Inazuma Japan's turn to kickoff!

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:57.970
The score is 4-2 with Storm Wolf in the lead!

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:00.640
Inazuma Japan has been driven into a corner!

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.130
2 points at the same time, huh?

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.110
Interesting. Let's try it!

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:08.320
They still haven't given up?

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:15.530
Minaho-kun!

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:18.240
Matatagi makes an unexpected back pass!

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:19.290
What?!

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:21.290
Ibuki-kun!

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:23.550
Move up!

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:30.430
Oh? All of Inazuma Japan is moving up the field!

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:32.880
It's a long pass!

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.140
We'll crush you before you can even start!

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:38.890
Storm Wolf also moves up, leaving their defenders behind!

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:40.270
Ibuki-kun!

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.270
We won't let you!

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:52.930
You're no match for me!

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:57.290
Minaho!

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:58.280
What?!

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:00.330
Shindou-kun!

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:01.960
Kusaka!

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.590
Nozaki!

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:07.340
Inazuma Japan is moving up bit by bit with their passes!

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.130
Sergei!

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:10.590
I'll stop you!

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:12.090
Oh no!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.760
Storm Wolf takes back the ball!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.020
Tetsukado!

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:27.230
If I don't want to be eaten up, look at everything without looking away.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.550
Footwork Draw!

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:38.410
Tetsukado!

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:40.660
Captain!

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:45.280
God Wind!

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:51.680
It's in!

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:54.640
Inazuma Japan's offense is a success!

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:57.350
Yes! Now we're back to being a point behind!

00:15:57.990 --> 00:15:58.860
Nii-chan!

00:15:58.860 --> 00:15:59.560
Yeah!

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:03.530
They had a clever scheme like that ready, huh?

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:06.660
But the score is 4-3 and we're in the lead.

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:10.320
We'll finish them with the next point.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.240
Move up!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.590
Now, it's time for our 2-points-at-the-same-time strategy!

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:20.950
Manabe-kun!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:27.460
3... 4... 5... 6...

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:28.710
Now!

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.040
Tsurugi steals back the ball!

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:36.050
Bicycle Sword!

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:39.140
What?!

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:40.640
His course is wide open!

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:41.890
Go back!

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:45.850
Unfortunately for you guys, you won't make it in time from where you're standing.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:48.590
Twi-

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.990
It's in!

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:58.030
I-Incredible! Inazuma Japan catches up to their second point almost immediately!

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:01.540
All right! We got 2 points at the same time!

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:05.250
Well, technically, it wasn't at the same time...

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:09.750
They were able to predict our movements?

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:11.480
All right!

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:15.760
An empty space after 6.70 seconds?

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:23.510
While I was watching them move, I noticed that when they go into offense formation, they always move the same way.

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:28.150
And once they begin moving, there's a moment exactly 6.70 seconds later...

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:33.280
...where no one is standing between the goal and the player possessing the ball.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.330
Then if we use that moment...

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:37.260
Yes.

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:40.310
First, we'll do whatever we can to take back the first point.

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:45.790
Then it's possible for us to use the 6.70 seconds that come afterwards to take our second point.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:52.570
We can't afford to lose. There's still time left.

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:55.010
This last play will make or break the game.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:58.760
Our remaining time is close to zero now!

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:06.230
Storm Wolf's Dmitri and Maxim move up the field with precise passes!

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:10.480
Will they end up shooting?!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.980
Which of them is it?

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.280
Minaho-kun, Tetsukado-kun!

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:16.360
They're here.

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:24.620
Storm Wolf's third forward has moved up!

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:27.540
Those two were just a decoy!

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:30.000
That defender can only cover a narrow range of defense.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.750
Bring these three towards us, and we can get past her!

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:33.750
Go!

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.000
It's mine!

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:37.910
Konoha!

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:53.940
S-She stops it!

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:56.440
W-What was that?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:59.240
I...

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:02.280
It has begun.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:04.950
Konoha!

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:07.750
Captain!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:08.910
Yuri!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.670
Z Slash!

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.000
Matatagi!

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.510
Parkour Attack!

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.390
Twist Reach!

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:37.280
It's in!

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:42.510
The end whistle has been blown!

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:56.060
With a score of 5-4, Inazuma Japan has made a miraculous turnabout victory at the last minute to win the FFI V2's Asia district preliminaries!

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.550
All right!

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.370
What happened to them?

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.120
What's going on?

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.210
What? What?!

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:42.670
What the heck is that?!

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:46.220
Storm Wolf is...

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:22.420
I-Is that...

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:24.480
...a spaceship?

00:22:54.100 --> 00:22:56.860
What were we fighting for all this time?

00:22:56.860 --> 00:23:00.140
What truths does the man who arrives bring us?

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:02.310
Super-dimensional goes on to the next stage!

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:03.560
Next, A Visitor!

00:23:03.750 --> 00:23:05.690
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.110 --> 00:23:19.570
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:26.820
Then we'll get 2 points at the same time!

00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:28.040
That's all!
